every event’s name and "},{"code":"tracked.records","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" every record."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Most code needs nothing more: it tracks through ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which falls back to the tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the app bootstrapped, and the test’s binding wins over that one. A view whose tracker was never set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that binds its tracker with ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reaches the test’s tracker too. Pass a tracker instead where the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"code reads one set for a single view tree. A tracker given to a SwiftUI view with ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracker(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", such as a preview’s,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reaches the view’s environment but not code that reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Such a test takes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker the body is given and sets it on the view: ","type":"text"},{"code":"withRecordingTracker { tracker in … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Typ